# Build context trimming for the mcpjam-inspector/Dockerfile image.
#
# Everything excluded here is NOT copied by any stage of
# mcpjam-inspector/Dockerfile, so it cannot change the built image — it only
# trims the payload Railway uploads. The excluded paths are the bulk of the
# tree: ~32 MB of documentation screenshots plus the GitHub automation.
#
# Do NOT add a `dist/` rule here. Unlike a normal package, this repository has
# a build artifact that is COMMITTED on purpose:
# mcpjam-inspector/server/services/browserd/dist/ is the prebuilt browserd
# daemon, which the image runs from the sandbox without ever building it.
# `server/services/browserd/__tests__/bundle-freshness.test.ts` and
# `npm run bundle:browserd` exist to keep it in sync. Excluding it produces an
# image whose browser tooling cannot start, and the failure looks unrelated.
#
# Likewise, keep the root package.json, package-lock.json and the package.json
# of all 13 workspaces: `npm ci --legacy-peer-deps` resolves the whole tree
# from that single lockfile, and `npm run build -w <pkg>` needs its neighbours
# present.

.git
.github
docs
notes

# Nothing in this repository commits dependencies, but a local `npm install`
# would otherwise upload a full node_modules tree as build context.
node_modules
**/node_modules

.DS_Store
*.log
